Release compliance rules

1. Recompute PackageReference and resolved package inventories before every
   release. Include new transitive packages, vendored code, generators, fonts,
   images, sounds, and other third-party materials.
2. Compare the release archive with Hatifect.Release.json. If any third-party
   file enters the archive, preserve its exact license and notices and reassess
   source and binary distribution duties.
3. For Apache-2.0 material, provide the license, mark modified files, preserve
   copyright/patent/trademark/attribution notices, and reproduce applicable
   NOTICE content as required by Apache License 2.0 Section 4.
4. Do not combine GPL- or AGPL-covered code into a Hatifect derivative without
   a separate compatibility review. For LGPL components, document the actual
   linking model and satisfy relinking, notice, source, and reverse-engineering
   conditions that apply to the distributed combination.
5. If a component is incompatible, replace it, keep it as a genuinely separate
   user-installed component, or change the licensing model after legal review.
6. Preserve the exact upstream license text from the reviewed revision in the
   release whenever its terms require distribution of that text. A URL in this
   source inventory is a verification aid, not a substitute where the license
   requires an accompanying copy.

This inventory is a technical record, not legal advice. Final compatibility,
notice, patent, and distribution conclusions must be reviewed by qualified
counsel before release.
